From cda36df249c201e1f2847ac2cda9337dcf52edfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:24:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HostFS: attributes as host xattrs, READDIRPLUS, idle nodes

- Attributes: a Haiku attribute is the host xattr "user.haiku.<name>"
  holding the type code (little endian) and the data, the convention of
  Haiku's build tools on the host; '/' and '%' in names are escaped the
  same way. Probed at mount (FUSE_LISTXATTR on the root); the "noattr"
  mount parameter turns them off. Files without a stored BEOS:TYPE get one
  from their extension (mime_ext_table, as on FAT), so Tracker shows the
  right icons without writing to the host. The volume says B_FS_HAS_MIME,
  and B_FS_HAS_ATTR when the host keeps xattrs (Apple's server does).
- Directories are read with FUSE_READDIRPLUS when the host offers it (it
  does): every entry comes with its node ID, so dirent.d_ino is the vnode ID
  the entry gets on lookup -- Tracker starts node monitoring from d_ino.
  The lookups the host counts for those entries go into the node table as
  soon as the reply arrives.
- Nodes nothing uses any more stay in the table as idle nodes (at most
  2048, oldest forgotten first) instead of being forgotten at once, so
  listing a directory does not cost a FORGET per entry, and a vnode the VFS
  drops is found again without a new lookup count.
---
 .../kernel/file_systems/hostfs/Jamfile        |   7 +-
 .../kernel/file_systems/hostfs/Volume.cpp     |  94 ++-
 .../kernel/file_systems/hostfs/attributes.cpp | 722 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../kernel/file_systems/hostfs/hostfs.h       |  45 ++
 .../file_systems/hostfs/kernel_interface.cpp  | 232 ++++--
 5 files changed, 1018 insertions(+), 82 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/hostfs/attributes.cpp

